# Agent skills (backend)

This repo is the **core API + data** (`:8080`, Java 21 / Spring Boot / JPA / OAuth2 resource server
/ Flyway / PostgreSQL). It is the **contract owner**: `frontend → bff → backend`.

## Skills this repo uses (from `claude-code-workflows` = `wshobson/agents`)

- `jvm-languages` — Spring Boot / Java 21 / layered architecture
- `database-design` — schema, queries, indexes, performance
- `database-migrations` — Flyway migrations
- `api-scaffolding` — REST endpoints / DTO contracts
- `backend-api-security` — Spring Security / OAuth2 resource server / JWT
- `security-scanning` — authz, injection, dependency CVEs, OWASP
- `qa-orchestra` — QA / test automation (Cursor & Claude; Codex uses `unit-testing` +
  `api-testing-observability`)
- `comprehensive-review` — multi-perspective code review

Planning / TDD / systematic debugging are process disciplines (Claude: `superpowers:*`) — apply
them regardless of agent.

## Using these in Cursor (2.5+)

Cursor has **no plugin CLI and no auto-install** (unlike Claude Code / Codex), so it's a one-time
manual step **inside the editor**:

1. Add the marketplace `wshobson/agents`.
2. `/plugin install <name>` for the skills above (Cursor generates `.cursor/rules/` +
   `.cursor-plugin/` pointing at the marketplace source).

Notes: Cursor does **not** honor a skill's `tools:` allowlist. The project auto-install (the
SessionStart hook, the launcher, `./skills`) only covers Claude/Codex — Cursor is manual.

## OpenAPI / Contract B (auto-generated)

Adding or changing a `@RestController` endpoint or a DTO **regenerates the OpenAPI spec
automatically** from annotations (springdoc serves `/swagger-ui.html` + `/v3/api-docs`) — there is
no hand-written spec, so no code↔spec drift. Annotate with `@Operation` / `@Schema` / `@Parameter`
/ `@ApiResponse`, keep the `@SecurityScheme` bearer JWT and the doc-path `permitAll` intact. CI
writes the spec to `target/openapi.json` during `./mvnw verify` and lints it with a **Spectral
gate** that requires every operation (summary/description/tags/response example) and every schema
field (description) to be documented. Run it locally with
`npx @stoplight/spectral-cli lint target/openapi.json`. See `docs/openapi-conventions.md`.

## Cross-repo rule (read before changing backend)

backend is the **contract origin** — a change to the REST contract / DTO / returned fields flows to
**bff** then **frontend**; prefer **additive/backward-compatible** changes. OAuth2 token changes
must agree with bff (`GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, audience/scope). Flyway migrations are **forward-only**.
The full Situation → skill table and cross-repo coordination rules are in `AGENTS.md` (Cursor reads
it).
